# Used by `vite build` only (Vite's production-mode env file), never by
# `vite dev` (which keeps using .env's absolute localhost:3000 URL, correct
# for its genuinely cross-origin dev setup: Vite on 5173, Backend on 3000).
#
# Relative, not absolute — this build gets served BY the Backend itself
# (see docs/offline-conversion-plan.md Phase 4: local static server, same
# origin as the API, reachable from other devices on the LAN). An absolute
# `http://localhost:3000/api` baked in here would break LAN access: a
# laptop loading this page from the host machine's LAN IP would still send
# API calls to ITS OWN localhost:3000 instead of the server's, since the
# URL is fixed at build time into the JS bundle. A relative path always
# resolves against whatever origin the browser actually loaded the page
# from — the host machine's IP or the Electron window's localhost, either
# way correct.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api
